  "description": "issue #679 (SP7): the spec's own canonical composition (spec/turtles-and-sprites.md:93-101) — `ask turtles [ each [ pen_up home pen_down ] ]` — proving the `turtles` reporter's result feeds `ask` directly. `turtles` reports the main turtle FIRST then each `new_turtle` in creation order, so `each` iterates id 0 then id 1 and every `pen-change`/`move`/`turn` carries that turtle's own `turtle_id`. `:friend` was moved to [0,30] by the preceding `tell`, so its `home` is a real move back to the origin, while the main turtle's is a no-op `move` [0,0]->[0,0] (`home` emits its `move`+`turn` pair unconditionally). The main turtle's events ARE stamped `turtle_id` 0 here, because `ask` has made the addressed set explicit. Every change of the addressed set — here from `ask`/`each`/`tell` — also emits the addressing `primitive` event carrying `addressing: { addressed_turtle_ids, current_turtle_id }`, so a consumer can identify the addressed turtle set (issue #766, spec/rendering.md:193); `ask`/`each` emit one again when the previous set is restored, on every exit path.",
